Date: Thu, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman_pcd: add CONFIG_FMAN_PCD_DEBUG_FS gate (0170)

Add the compile-time gate for the fman_pcd debugfs surface.  The
production control plane is the generic-netlink "ask" family plus the
exported fman_pcd_* kernel API; debugfs is a bring-up diagnostic only
and must be absent from production images (plans/ASK2-PRODUCTION-
ARCHITECTURE.md Phase 1).

The symbol is consumed by F-191 (bin/kernel-fixups/F_191.py), which
wraps the debugfs registration block in fman_pcd.c with
`if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_FMAN_PCD_DEBUG_FS))`.  `default n` means the
nodes are compiled out (dead-code eliminated) unless a dev kernel
explicitly enables the option.

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/Kconfig b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/Kconfig
index 5d204b7..aa71ecd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/Kconfig
@@ -50,3 +50,19 @@ config FSL_FMAN_PCD
 	  rate. This skeleton delivers the orchestration scaffold; the
 	  per-engine APIs land in follow-up patches.
 	  If unsure, say Y.
+
+config FMAN_PCD_DEBUG_FS
+	bool "FMan PCD debugfs diagnostics (dev/bring-up only)"
+	depends on FSL_FMAN_PCD && DEBUG_FS
+	default n
+	help
+	  Expose /sys/kernel/debug/fman_pcd/<id>/ diagnostic nodes
+	  (fe_arm, fe_flow, fe_ehash, muram_budget, ...) for silicon
+	  bring-up and development.
+
+	  This is NOT a production interface. Production images MUST
+	  disable this option so no fman_pcd debugfs nodes exist; the
+	  production control surface is the generic-netlink "ask" family
+	  and the fman_pcd_* kernel API.
+
+	  Say N in production. Say Y when iterating on hardware.
